#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-archimport.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "git-archimport(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-archimport.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-archimport.txt:7
msgid "git-archimport - Import a GNU Arch repository into Git"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-archimport.txt:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-archimport.txt:14
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"'git archimport' [-h] [-v] [-o] [-a] [-f] [-T] [-D <depth>] [-t <tempdir>]\n"
"\t       <archive>/<branch>[:<git-branch>]...\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-archimport.txt:16
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-archimport.txt:23
msgid ""
"Imports a project from one or more GNU Arch repositories.  It will follow "
"branches and repositories within the namespaces defined by the "
"<archive>/<branch> parameters supplied. If it cannot find the remote branch "
"a merge comes from it will just import it as a regular commit. If it can "
"find it, it will mark it as a merge whenever possible (see discussion "
"below)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-archimport.txt:27
msgid ""
"The script expects you to provide the key roots where it can start the "
"import from an 'initial import' or 'tag' type of Arch commit. It will follow "
"and import new branches within the provided roots."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-archimport.txt:32
msgid ""
"It expects to be dealing with one project only. If it sees branches that "
"have different roots, it will refuse to run. In that case, edit your "
"<archive>/<branch> parameters to define clearly the scope of the import."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-archimport.txt:37
msgid ""
"'git archimport' uses `tla` extensively in the background to access the Arch "
"repository.  Make sure you have a recent version of `tla` available in the "
"path. `tla` must know about the repositories you pass to 'git archimport'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-archimport.txt:42
msgid ""
"For the initial import, 'git archimport' expects to find itself in an empty "
"directory. To follow the development of a project that uses Arch, rerun 'git "
"archimport' with the same parameters as the initial import to perform "
"incremental imports."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-archimport.txt:49
msgid ""
"While 'git archimport' will try to create sensible branch names for the "
"archives that it imports, it is also possible to specify Git branch names "
"manually.  To do so, write a Git branch name after each <archive>/<branch> "
"parameter, separated by a colon.  This way, you can shorten the Arch branch "
"names and convert Arch jargon to Git jargon, for example mapping a "
"\"PROJECT{litdd}devo{litdd}VERSION\" branch to \"master\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-archimport.txt:54
msgid ""
"Associating multiple Arch branches to one Git branch is possible; the result "
"will make the most sense only if no commits are made to the first branch, "
"after the second branch is created.  Still, this is useful to convert Arch "
"repositories that had been rotated periodically."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-archimport.txt:57
#, no-wrap
msgid "MERGES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-archimport.txt:63
msgid ""
"Patch merge data from Arch is used to mark merges in Git as well. Git does "
"not care much about tracking patches, and only considers a merge when a "
"branch incorporates all the commits since the point they forked. The end "
"result is that Git will have a good idea of how far branches have "
"diverged. So the import process does lose some patch-trading metadata."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-archimport.txt:67
msgid ""
"Fortunately, when you try and merge branches imported from Arch, Git will "
"find a good merge base, and it has a good chance of identifying patches that "
"have been traded out-of-sequence between the branches."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-archimport.txt:69
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-archimport.txt:73
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-h::`\n"
"\tDisplay usage.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-archimport.txt:76
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-v::`\n"
"\tVerbose output.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-archimport.txt:80
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-T::`\n"
"\tMany tags. Will create a tag for every commit, reflecting the commit\n"
"\tname in the Arch repository.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-archimport.txt:85
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-f::`\n"
"\tUse the fast patchset import strategy.  This can be significantly\n"
"\tfaster for large trees, but cannot handle directory renames or\n"
"\tpermissions changes.  The default strategy is slow and safe.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-archimport.txt:93
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-o::`\n"
"\tUse this for compatibility with old-style branch names used by\n"
"\tearlier versions of 'git archimport'.  Old-style branch names\n"
"\twere category{litdd}branch, whereas new-style branch names are\n"
"\tarchive,category{litdd}branch{litdd}version.  In both cases, names given\n"
"\ton the command-line will override the automatically-generated\n"
"\tones.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-archimport.txt:98
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-D`\n"
"\tFollow merge ancestry and attempt to import trees that have been\n"
"\tmerged from.  Specify a depth greater than 1 if patch logs have been\n"
"\tpruned.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-archimport.txt:102
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-a::`\n"
"\tAttempt to auto-register archives at `http://mirrors.sourcecontrol.net`\n"
"\tThis is particularly useful with the -D option.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-archimport.txt:105
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-t`\n"
"\tOverride the default tempdir.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-archimport.txt:107
#, no-wrap
msgid "<archive>/<branch>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-archimport.txt:109
msgid "<archive>/<branch> identifier in a format that `tla log` understands."
msgstr ""

